WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.504
OSINT draws from many public source categories, each with different strengths and limitations.

00:00:05.504 --> 00:00:10.492
Search engines help discover material, but their results are ranked, incomplete, personalized,

00:00:10.492 --> 00:00:12.155
and subject to change.

00:00:12.155 --> 00:00:17.559
Analysts should treat search results as discovery aids rather than evidence by themselves.

00:00:17.559 --> 00:00:22.547
Websites and official public records can provide direct statements, filings, policies, notices,

00:00:22.547 --> 00:00:23.794
and historical context.

00:00:23.794 --> 00:00:28.366
News organizations and specialist publications may add reporting and expert interpretation.

00:00:28.366 --> 00:00:33.354
Forums and social platforms can surface early observations, but identity, authenticity, motive,

00:00:33.354 --> 00:00:35.848
and context often require careful validation.

00:00:35.848 --> 00:00:42.499
Domain and DNS data can help describe public-facing infrastructure and relationships at a point in time.

00:00:42.499 --> 00:00:46.240
Code repositories may expose public project history, dependencies, documentation,

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:47.488
or security advisories.

00:00:47.488 --> 00:00:51.644
Collection must remain within lawful public access and organizational policy;

00:00:51.644 --> 00:00:55.801
public-source work never authorizes access to private repositories or accounts.

00:00:55.801 --> 00:01:00.789
Images and video may contain visible objects, text, landmarks, weather, shadows, edits,

00:01:00.789 --> 00:01:02.036
or publication metadata.

00:01:02.036 --> 00:01:05.777
Maps and geospatial sources can help test location claims.

00:01:05.777 --> 00:01:12.013
Visual analysis should avoid identifying or tracking private individuals without lawful authority and a legitimate,

00:01:12.013 --> 00:01:12.844
proportionate purpose.

00:01:12.844 --> 00:01:15.338
Source selection should follow the requirement.

00:01:15.338 --> 00:01:19.079
Official records may be strong for a legal filing,

00:01:19.079 --> 00:01:23.652
while direct technical documentation may be better for a software behavior.

00:01:23.652 --> 00:01:29.887
A social post may provide a lead but not enough support for a consequential judgment.

00:01:29.887 --> 00:01:34.459
Maintain a source inventory that records ownership, access conditions, update patterns,

00:01:34.459 --> 00:01:36.538
expected reliability, and preservation needs.

00:01:36.538 --> 00:01:37.369
Diversity matters:

00:01:37.369 --> 00:01:44.020
independent sources with different origins provide stronger corroboration than many sites repeating the same original claim.
